        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9la9dr-5gsd40eg",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Cusco"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_label:64b40b4997a74d9e",
      "field": "itinerary.label",
      "sourceTextSha256": "93918da548154ed9157a2b3f63138aadbebf123c03985f778e93de1ce9d23f3b",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9la9dr-5gsd40eg",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Puno and Lake Titicaca"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:a8556f49d5a8d777",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "39c6cd606630d25b2a0366ee2409fa617fe526b944a788c629d39b0db35756e0",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9la9dr-5gsd40eg",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Have breakfast at the hotel, then take the bus from Cusco to Puno.\n\nThe journey takes almost all day and includes several stops.\n\nYour first stop is **Andahuaylillas**, where you’ll see why it draws comparisons with the Sistine Chapel.\n\nNext, visit **Raqchi**, an ancient complex that served an administrative function in Inca times.\n\nAfter lunch in **Sicuani**, continue to **La Raya**, one of the highest points on the road. There’s a market here against a mountain backdrop.\n\nYou’ll also stop at **Pucará**, an ancient Inca fortification.\n\nAfter about **10 hours on the road**, arrive in Puno and check in at the **3-star Sol Plaza** or a similar hotel."
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_title:146220931af7d21d",
      "field": "contentBlock.title",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2d74e5169fa4ef6c18724dd801c85a73ad82dddaf448642b3a0e7c3b18bc7e99",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9la9dr-5gsd40eg",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "Optional: Titicaca Train"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:contentBlock_text:26f50251e177951e",
      "field": "contentBlock.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "f426cdc7af022eeb60ccad6c0ad5f02bec16e9760706c2cd5d9e10e474939453",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-20261109-mw9la9dr-5gsd40eg",
        "model": "gpt-6.1-sol"
      },
      "text": "You can take the luxury **Titicaca Train** from Cusco to Puno instead of travelling by bus.\n\nThe train runs on **Wednesdays, Fridays and Sundays**. Along the way, you can watch the changing mountain scenery.\n\nLunch in the dining car includes a starter, a main course and dessert. Wine is available to order at the bar.\n\nThe train stops at **La Raya**, the highest point on the route, at **4,319 metres**.\n\nArrive in Puno at around **19:00**.\n\n**Supplement:** $250 per person."
    }
  ]
